CLI


AWS CLI Practical Guide & Notes (DevOps/Cloud Engineer)

AWS CLI is one of the most important tools for DevOps Engineers because it allows you to automate AWS operations from Linux, Windows, Jenkins, GitLab CI, GitHub Actions, Ansible, and Shell Scripts.



1. Install AWS CLI

Linux
	curl "https://awscli.amazonaws.com/awscli-exe-linux-x86_64.zip" -o "awscliv2.zip"

	unzip awscliv2.zip

	sudo ./aws/install

	aws --version

Output:

	aws-cli/2.x.x



2. Configure AWS CLI


	aws configure

	Enter:

		AWS Access Key ID
		AWS Secret Access Key
		Region
		
		Output Format

			Example:

			Access Key: AKIA*******
			Secret Key: *********
			Region: ap-south-1
			Output: json


3. Verify Credentials

	aws sts get-caller-identity

Output:

	{
	  "UserId": "ABC123",
	  "Account": "123456789012",
	  "Arn": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:user/admin"
	}


4. AWS CLI Profiles

		Create multiple accounts.

	aws configure --profile dev

	aws configure --profile prod

Use profile:

	aws s3 ls --profile prod

	List profiles:

		cat ~/.aws/config
		cat ~/.aws/credentials


5. Common Output Formats

	JSON

		aws ec2 describe-instances

	Table

		aws ec2 describe-instances --output table

	Text

		aws ec2 describe-instances --output text




7. S3 Practical Commands
	

	List Buckets

		aws s3 ls

	Create Bucket

		aws s3 mb s3://my-devops-bucket
	
	Delete Bucket
		
		aws s3 rb s3://my-devops-bucket

	Upload File
	
		aws s3 cp backup.zip s3://mybucket/

	Download File
	
		aws s3 cp s3://mybucket/backup.zip .

	Sync Folder

	Upload

		aws s3 sync ./data s3://mybucket/data

	Download

		aws s3 sync s3://mybucket/data ./data

	Delete Object

		aws s3 rm s3://mybucket/test.txt




8. EC2 Practical Commands

	List Instances

		aws ec2 describe-instances

	Launch Instance
	
		aws ec2 run-instances \
			--image-id ami-123456 \
			--instance-type t2.micro \
			--key-name mykey

	Start Instance
	
		aws ec2 start-instances \
			--instance-ids i-123456

	Stop Instance

		aws ec2 stop-instances \
			--instance-ids i-123456

	Reboot

		aws ec2 reboot-instances \

			--instance-ids i-123456
	
	Terminate

		aws ec2 terminate-instances \
			--instance-ids i-123456


9. Security Groups

	List SGs

		aws ec2 describe-security-groups

	Create SG

		aws ec2 create-security-group \
		--group-name web-sg \
		--description "Web Access"

	Open Port 22

		aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress \
		--group-id sg-12345 \
		--protocol tcp \
		--port 22 \
		--cidr 0.0.0.0/0

	Open Port 80

		aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress \
		--group-id sg-12345 \
		--protocol tcp \
		--port 80 \
		--cidr 0.0.0.0/0


10. EBS Practical

	Create Volume

		aws ec2 create-volume \
		--size 20 \
		--availability-zone ap-south-1a

	Attach Volume

		aws ec2 attach-volume \
		--volume-id vol-123 \
		--instance-id i-123 \
		--device /dev/xvdf

	List Volumes

		aws ec2 describe-volumes


11. Snapshot Commands

	Create Snapshot

		aws ec2 create-snapshot \
		--volume-id vol-123 \
		--description "Daily Backup"

	List Snapshots

		aws ec2 describe-snapshots \
		--owner-ids self

	Delete Snapshot

		aws ec2 delete-snapshot \
		--snapshot-id snap-123

12. IAM Commands

	List Users

		aws iam list-users

	Create User

		aws iam create-user \
		--user-name devops

	Create Access Key

		aws iam create-access-key \
		--user-name devops

	Attach Policy

		aws iam attach-user-policy \
		--user-name devops \
		--policy-arn arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AdministratorAccess


14. Load Balancer Commands

	List ALB

		aws elbv2 describe-load-balancers

	List Target Groups

		aws elbv2 describe-target-groups

	List Targets

		aws elbv2 describe-target-health \
		--target-group-arn arn


15. Route53 Commands

	List Hosted Zones

		aws route53 list-hosted-zones

	List Records

		aws route53 list-resource-record-sets \
		--hosted-zone-id Z12345


16. RDS Commands

	List Databases

		aws rds describe-db-instances

	Start RDS

		aws rds start-db-instance \
		--db-instance-identifier mydb

	Stop RDS

		aws rds stop-db-instance \
		--db-instance-identifier mydb


17. CloudWatch Commands

	List Metrics

		aws cloudwatch list-metrics

	Get CPU Usage

		aws cloudwatch get-metric-statistics \
		--namespace AWS/EC2 \
		--metric-name CPUUtilization


18. Lambda Commands

	List Functions

		aws lambda list-functions

	Invoke Function

		aws lambda invoke \
		--function-name myfunction \
		output.json




19. ECR Commands

	Login

		aws ecr get-login-password \
		| docker login \
		--username AWS \
		--password-stdin ACCOUNT_ID.dkr.ecr.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com

	Create Repository

		aws ecr create-repository \
		--repository-name myapp

	Push Image

		docker push ACCOUNT_ID.dkr.ecr.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/myapp:v1
	

20. ECS Commands

	List Clusters

		aws ecs list-clusters

	List Services

		aws ecs list-services \
		--cluster mycluster




21. Useful DevOps Commands

	Get Current Region

		aws configure get region

	Get Account ID

		aws sts get-caller-identity \
		--query Account \
		--output text

	List All Regions

		aws ec2 describe-regions \
		--query "Regions[*].RegionName"



AWS CLI Interview Questions


Q1. Difference between AWS CLI and SDK?

	CLI → Command Line
	SDK → Programming Language API


Q2. Where are credentials stored?

Linux:

	~/.aws/credentials
	~/.aws/config



Q3. How do you assume an IAM Role?


	aws sts assume-role \
	--role-arn arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/AdminRole \
	--role-session-name DevOpsSession


Q4. How do you debug AWS CLI commands?


	aws s3 ls --debug


Q5. How do you use CLI in Jenkins?


	stage('Deploy') {
	    steps {
	        sh 'aws s3 sync build/ s3://prod-bucket'
	    }
	}



